@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 安装：前提：DSH `0.2.0` 系列（`0.2.0-rc.1` 及之后，见「兼容性」）；Node `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`；`dsh` 与 `pnpm` 可用。

> **路由互斥**：同一个 profile 里 `opencode-go` 只能由一个适配器提供。装本插件前请先卸载旧插件（`dsh plugin --profile <p> remove @dan-ai-studio/dsh-opencode-go`），或清空 `llm-pi-ai` 配置里名为 `opencode-go` 的 provider。否则插件会记录一条明确的占用诊断，路由不会注册（其余功能照常）。

> **桌面端用户**：DSH 桌面端不走命令行安装，安装、升级与卸载都在应用内 Plugins 页完成，见文末「桌面端（Electron 应用）」。

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 方式二：GitHub Release：```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego/releases/download/v<版本>/dan-ai-studio-dshopencodego-<版本>.tgz
```

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 配置：API Key 通过 Harness 凭证库提供（引用名 `OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY`），也可以直接 `export OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY=...`。

**流超时**：`streamIdleTimeoutMs` 约束的是**两次流事件之间的最长静默**，不是请求总时长——长思考模型只要持续产出事件就不会被误判。默认 5 分钟，上限为 `2147483647`（约 24.8 天）。超时抛出 `TIMEOUT`（可重试类）。

**连接保留**：`keepAliveTimeoutMs` 决定**与网关的连接在两次请求之间保留多久**。计时器**每次收到回答后重新开始**，所以常用时连接不会被断开，它约束的只是两次请求之间的静默。默认 10 分钟。

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 配置：**工具声明**：每个请求都发送当前完整的工具列表。宿主提供的会话折叠历史（`toolHistory`）**故意不投影**：投影需要路由声明 `toolUpdate` 模式，而 models.dev 对本网关模型只声明"可调用工具"、没有声明该模式；凭空声明会让模型看到的东西悄悄改变。

**重试**：`retryPolicy` 是可选的，不写就用宿主默认。写了就由可选的 `dsh-llm-retry` 插件执行，配置错误在写入时报错而不是等到失败发生。

**固定 IP**：`pinnedAddresses` 把网关域名固定到一个地址，用来接入更近的边缘节点（系统解析到的边缘有时离得很远，而每个请求都要为那段距离付费）。

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 兼容性：**支持**：DSH `0.2.0` 系列（`0.2.0-rc.1` 及之后的正式版）与 `0.2.1` 系列。插件在 `engines.dsh` 与每个 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` 的 `peerDependencies` 上声明 `>=0.2.0-rc.1 <0.3.0-0`。

**不再支持 `0.2.0` 之前**：`0.1.7` 系列及更早的版本自 v0.1.36 起被移除支持——那段范围内的运行时接口与本插件当前依赖的接口已经不同，继续声明只会让门禁放行一个未经验证的组合。`0.1.8`、`0.1.9` 从未发布。

**机制（不是写死）**：DSH 在挂载插件前会读取插件 `package.json` 的声明，对**运行时的 DSH 版本**做 semver 判定（含预发布，即 `includePrerelease`）。判定分两级，先命中先赢：

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 兼容性：1. **`engines.dsh` 优先且独占**：插件只要声明了它，就**只**由它决定，`peerDependencies` 完全不参与判定（DSH 源码 `packages/boot/app-boot/src/plugin-compatibility.ts`：命中 `engines.dsh` 即返回）。
2. 插件**没有**声明 `engines.dsh` 时，才逐个检查 `@deepseek-ai/dsh` / `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` 的 peer 范围。

判定结果：

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · 兼容性：- 满足 → 正常加载；
- 不满足 → **该插件行被禁用并打印原因**（`Plugin … is incompatible with dsh …`），其他插件不受影响；
- 需要冒险时可用**精确版本豁免**：`dsh plugin --profile <profile> allow-version <包>@<版本> --dsh-version <精确版本> --accept-risk`（只对该包与该精确版本生效）；`dsh plugin --profile <profile> version-exemptions` 可列出当前 profile 的豁免。

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · Option 2: GitHub Release：```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego/releases/download/v<version>/dan-ai-studio-dshopencodego-<version>.tgz
```

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · Desktop (Electron app)：Installation **must** go through the in-app UI — do not use the `dsh plugin` commands above:

1. Open the Desktop app → **Settings → Plugins**;
2. Enter `@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego` as the install spec (or pin a version, e.g. `@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego@0.1.11`), and confirm;
3. **Restart the app** when prompted, then enter the API key on the settings page (reference name `OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY`).

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · A common question: does the provider adding or retiring a model need a plugin release?：- a model the provider **adds** appears on the next refresh; if no metadata source describes it, it is labelled as inferred and can be pinned with `modelProtocols`;
- a model the provider **retires** disappears on the next refresh;
- the bundled catalog is **frozen at the plugin's version** and affects only the quality of the "how to call it" decision, never *which* models exist.
- **fresh installs do not wait**: the bundle carries a directory snapshot from publish time (`src/catalog/seed.snapshot.json`), which answers at once when the disk cache is empty and refreshes behind it; past 24 hours without a refresh counts as stale and refreshes in the background too, whatever the TTL says. A timer re-checks on a live host, so long-running processes stay current without a request to trigger it.

@dan-ai-studio/dshopencodego README · The model list in the settings page：- **context / max input / max output**, **release date**, **price per 1M tokens** (from models.dev), and **Go allowance**;
- **Go allowance** is fetched at runtime from the provider's own documentation — the "usage limits / estimated requests" tables, whose source is a markdown file in the provider's repository (GitHub first, jsDelivr second) — and refreshes with the catalog every 60 minutes. A failed fetch keeps the last successful parse; a process that never succeeded uses the **built-in snapshot** and the page says so, with the transcription date (`src/go-limits.ts`, frozen, not maintained by hand). A moved or restructured document counts as a failed fetch, never as an emptied column;
- **Input modalities**: a separate line lists the input modes models.dev declares (text / image / audio / video / PDF). These are the **model's own metadata**, not what the Harness can forward — the Harness sends text and images natively; audio/video/PDF travel as attachments and tool reads. The line is absent when the document declares none.
